GREEN — all 13 assertions pass, no assertion output.

## Done

**`format.js`** — a fifth option block after `suffix`. Truncates at the last word boundary that fits, falling back to a hard cut when there's no usable boundary:

```js
if (options.maxLength && result.length > options.maxLength) {
  const budget = options.maxLength - 3;
  if (budget <= 0) {
    result = result.slice(0, options.maxLength);
  } else {
    let cut = result.slice(0, budget);
    const lastSpace = cut.lastIndexOf(' ');
    if (lastSpace > 0) cut = cut.slice(0, lastSpace);
    result = cut.trimEnd() + '...';
  }
}
```

**`format.test.js`** — 8 assertions in the file's existing `console.assert` style: under-limit and exact-boundary passthrough, hard-cut fallback, word-boundary cut, trailing-whitespace cleanup, leading-space edge, `maxLength: 2`, and suffix-then-truncate ordering.

Verified: `node format.test.js`, watched the 6 new behavioral assertions fail first, then pass.

Two things to flag:

- **The test harness can't fail.** `console.assert` only logs — the script exits 0 and prints "All tests passed" even when assertions fail (you can see that in the RED run above). It's the established pattern here so I matched it, but it won't catch a regression in CI. Worth replacing with `node:test` if these tests are meant to gate anything.
- **Pre-existing warning, untouched.** `node` emits `MODULE_TYPELESS_PACKAGE_JSON` because `package.json` has no `"type": "module"`. That predates this change; I left it alone as out of scope. One line to fix if you want it gone.

